                    {
                        "sense_id": "7b6ed342-a06e-3f8d-8bf7-962514ef981d",
                        "entry_id": "a30033f0-bedd-3866-bc57-67e43a11bb47",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An inhabitant of pre-Hellenic Greece."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a0cfc1a-4b42-4633-aef3-b75dae9dcec8",
                                "sense_id": "7b6ed342-a06e-3f8d-8bf7-962514ef981d",
                                "text": "It seems evident that the Hellenes much excelled the Pelasgians in the spirit of enterprise and in military accomplishments."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3c65a2f-2ca8-41f0-82bb-fc1d744cc357",
                                "sense_id": "7b6ed342-a06e-3f8d-8bf7-962514ef981d",
                                "text": "In Homer the Pelasgians¹ are of little importance. They are inhabitants of Asia Minor, where they possess a Larissa, and fight in the ranks of the Trojan army. We also hear of Pelasgi among the inhabitants of Crete."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
